        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-8" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Degree minutes are used to calculate the heating deficit for radiators or floor heating.&lt;div&gt;(If your floor needs 30c, but only is 29c for 1 minute, you lose 1 dm)&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="74.5" width="240" x="2665" y="262.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-9" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="The house temperature is controlled by &lt;b&gt;degree minutes&lt;/b&gt;.&amp;nbsp;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="37" width="190" x="2690" y="188.88" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-10" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="The compressor starts when degree minutes reach -60 (by default), each step of the electric element is even more negative&lt;div&gt;(can be changed)&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="76" width="240" x="2665" y="352.97" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-11" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="The hot water temperature is controlled by&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;start&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;stop&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;temperature&lt;/b&gt; logic." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="51.12" width="190" x="2990" y="188.88000000000002" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-13" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;How it works?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30.2" width="135" x="3007.5" y="257.78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-14" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The F1155 monitors the hot water tank with a temperature sensor (bt6, which is put in the water tank)&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="47.5" width="240" x="2955" y="374.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-16" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;When the temperature in the tank drops below the set &quot;&lt;b&gt;Start temperature&lt;/b&gt;&quot; it begins heating the tank until the tank reaches the set &quot;&lt;b&gt;Stop temperature&lt;/b&gt;&quot;.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="69.12" width="240" x="2955" y="282.56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-18" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;line-height: 100%; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Economy (45/51°C),&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;line-height: 100%; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;Normal (49/55°C),&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;line-height: 100%; font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;Luxury (52/58°C)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="57" width="163.75" x="2997.5" y="461.13" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-19" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffcd28;gradientColor=#ffa500;strokeColor=#d79b00;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 22px;&quot;&gt;How Do They Work Together?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="580" x="2640" y="780" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-20" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fad7ac;strokeColor=#b46504;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="311.89" width="580" x="2640" y="818.1100000000001" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-21" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 13px;&quot;&gt;The compressor and heating element are used for &lt;b&gt;both&lt;/b&gt; heating your water and your house.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="27.26" width="547.5" x="2652.5" y="826.8499999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-24" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="A &lt;b&gt;shuttle valve&lt;/b&gt; (QN10) is used to control where the heat goes" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="103.55" width="137" x="2652.5" y="877" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-25" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;When the tanks temperature is too low the shuttle valve moves to the hot water position, so the hot liquid (water with additives) coming out of the compressor stops going to your floors and radiator and starts flowing through a coil inside your water tank. Once the stop temperature is hit the valve flips back.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="79.13" width="400" x="2800" y="908.8699999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-26" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Heat inside the heat pump is transfered using a closed liquid loop, for both house and water warming." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="34.05" width="400" x="2800" y="865.95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-28" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#b0e3e6;strokeColor=#0e8088;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Priority&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="25.56" width="135" x="2862.5" y="1002.3899999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-29" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;The F1155 can only do one thing at a time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;It can either be heating your water or your house.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="40" width="263.75" x="2798.13" y="1027.54" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-30" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;By default F1155 gives hot water priority, but this means that the house can start colling while you heat the tank.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="50" width="263.75" x="2798.13" y="1067.54" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-31" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;line-height: 110%;&quot;&gt;Some Very Rough Calculations&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="27.26" width="185" x="2692.5" y="449.07" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-32" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=1" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 11px;&quot;&gt;For a standard 100m^2 Dutch row house it takes around 2-5 kWh to raise the air and wall temperature by 1c.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="57.86" width="200" x="2685" y="476.14" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-33" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=1" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Once the house is at 20c, to keep the temperature you need 0.5 - 1.5 kW of continuous power when it is 0c outside.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="57.86" width="200" x="2685" y="533.25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-35" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=1" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;(it take 0.25 - 0.75 Kw if it is 10c outside)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="28.89" width="200" x="2685" y="591.11" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-36" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Heating Modes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="27.26" width="127.5" x="3015.62" y="433.87" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-37" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The default start and stop temperatures can be changed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="35.37" width="163.75" x="2997.5" y="518.13" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-38" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#b1ddf0;strokeColor=#10739e;" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Heating Steps&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
