        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-40" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#cce5ff;strokeColor=#36393d;" value="1. Block Compressor&lt;div&gt;2. Increase the heating curve by 1c&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;3.Based on the available overproduction set DM to turn on/off the heating elements.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. Stop heating when the current temperature hits the heating curves max (dm starts going positive)&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110.14" width="290" x="2640" y="669.86" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="aeWKPAIoGOQ0hn3melRO-41" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fad9d5;strokeColor=#ae4132;" value="1. Block Compressor&lt;div&gt;2. Set Lux stop temperature to 75c&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. When overproduction is detected start Lux mode&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;(if needed set Lux start temp to 1c bellow current)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;4. Cap the powerdraw of elements based on the overproduction&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
